 careful of duplicates). Let me check payments-worker first, and maybe list incidents to see if the incident was created.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150bf342b7f30a15aed61", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-worker\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a150bf342b7f30a15aed77", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-worker\"}", "name": "list_deployments"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a150bf342b7f30a15aed8a", "function": {"arguments": "{}", "name": "list_incidents"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "Confirmed: **payments-worker** is running v3.4.0 (unhealthy, 18% error rate) and its most recent healthy release is **v3.3.0**. Rolling back now and opening the SEV2 incident (the earlier incident request timed out before creating anything).", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150bf397b7451b56272e7", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-worker\",\"version\":\"v3.3.0\"}", "name": "rollback"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a150bf397b7451b56272f3", "function": {"arguments": "{\"idempotency_key\":\"payments-worker-v3.4.0-errors-rollback\",\"service\":\"payments-worker\",\"severity\":\"SEV2\",\"summary\":\"payments-worker error rate spiked to 18% after the v3.4.0 deploy; service unhealthy across us-east, us-west, and eu-west. Rolling back to last known healthy release v3.3.0.\",\"title\":\"Payments worker elevated error rate following v3.4.0 deploy\"}", "name": "create_incident"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": null, "reasoning_content": "Done. Verify service status? Could confirm health after rollback. Quick check.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150bf3c9774b197b15f22", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-worker\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "stop", "content": "Done. Summary:\n\n- **Identified the problem:** `payments-api` was also unhealthy, but a reviewer clarified the actual affected service is **payments-worker**, which was on v3.4.0 with an 18% error rate (unhealthy across us-east, us-west, and eu-west).\n- **Rolled back** payments-worker to v3.3.0, its most recent version that was healthy in production (change-manager approved).\n- **Opened SEV2 incident** INC-0002 \"Payments worker elevated error rate following v3.4.0 deploy\" \u2014 the on-call engineer has been paged.\n- **Verified recovery:** payments-worker is now healthy on v3.3.0 with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n\nNote: payments-api also showed an unhealthy v5.1.0 deploy (18% error rate) \u2014 I attempted a rollback there first but it was denied as the wrong service, so I did not proceed on that one. You may want to confirm with the team whether payments-api needs attention too, or whether its errors were downstream of the worker.", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": []}]}